WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.326
In 1996, Taiwan held a special election.

00:00:04.326 --> 00:00:07.729
It was the first time voters directly elected the president.

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:10.825
Colorful flags filled the streets in a lively atmosphere.

00:00:10.825 --> 00:00:14.508
Candidates traveled everywhere to speak and win support.

00:00:14.508 --> 00:00:17.525
The plaza was packed with people listening to speeches.

00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:20.717
Some came with their whole families to listen.

00:00:20.717 --> 00:00:24.504
Early on voting day, long lines formed at polling stations.

00:00:24.504 --> 00:00:27.919
Each person held their own ballot in hand.

00:00:27.919 --> 00:00:30.720
Ballots were cast one by one into the ballot box.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:34.492
This vote would decide the future leader.

00:00:34.492 --> 00:00:37.727
Young people voting for the first time were especially excited.

00:00:37.727 --> 00:00:41.108
As votes were counted, everyone watched the results closely.

00:00:41.108 --> 00:00:45.673
Television and radio kept bringing the latest news.

00:00:45.673 --> 00:00:48.533
No matter whom they supported, everyone respected the result.

00:00:48.533 --> 00:00:52.112
The election ended peacefully, and a new president was chosen.

00:00:52.112 --> 00:00:54.913
It was an important milestone in Taiwan's democratic development.
